FAE API spec — First Atoms Engine Simulation Framework

Core concepts

Engine: Atomic‑gradient propulsion simulator (FAE)

Domain: Atomic stability fields, fusion anchors, entropy reinforcement, drift evaluation

Style: Modular, field‑based, time‑stepped simulation

1. Data structures

EnvState

Fields:

C(t): cosmic telemetry stream

S(t, λ): spectral density

Z_env: environmental atomic composition

AnchorState

Fields:

F_PtU(t): Pt/U fusion state vector

M_conf(t): MHD confinement parameters

Psi_core(t): core coherence state

FieldState

Fields:

Phi_ext(t, x): external atomic stability field

Phi_int(t, x): internal atomic anchor field

GradPhi(t, x): raw gradient

GradPhi_star(t, x): reinforced gradient

EntropyState

Fields:

E_spike(t): fusion energy spike magnitude

S_A(t): atomic‑scale entropy term

DriftState

Fields:

v_eff(t, x): effective drift velocity field

a_eff(t, x): effective acceleration field

2. Module APIs

2.1 Environment ingest

Function: ingest_environment()

Inputs: raw cosmic telemetry, spectral data, Z_env

Outputs: EnvState

Description: Normalizes and packages environmental/astrophysical inputs.

2.2 Fusion anchor ingest

Function: ingest_anchor()

Inputs: fusion diagnostics, MHD parameters, core coherence metrics

Outputs: AnchorState

Description: Encodes Pt/U fusion anchor and confinement state.

2.3 Field construction

Function: build_fields(env: EnvState, anchor: AnchorState)

Inputs: EnvState, AnchorState

Outputs: FieldState (with Phi_ext, Phi_int)

Description: Computes external and internal atomic stability fields.

2.4 Gradient solver

Function: solve_gradient(fields: FieldState)

Inputs: FieldState

Outputs: updated FieldState (with GradPhi)

Description: Applies MHD, Coulomb modulation, and atomic flux coupling to refine and compute ∇Φ_A.

2.5 Entropy engine

Function: compute_entropy(anchor: AnchorState)

Inputs: AnchorState

Outputs: EntropyState

Description: Detects fusion spikes and converts them to atomic‑scale entropy S_A.

Function: reinforce_gradient(fields: FieldState, entropy: EntropyState)

Inputs: FieldState, EntropyState

Outputs: updated FieldState (with GradPhi_star)

Description: Applies entropy reinforcement to the gradient.

2.6 Drift evaluation

Function: evaluate_drift(fields: FieldState, entropy: EntropyState)

Inputs: FieldState, EntropyState

Outputs: DriftState

Description: Computes v_eff and a_eff under the constraint v_eff < c.

3. Kernel orchestration

Function: run_fae_step(t)

Inputs: time t, raw environment and anchor data

Outputs: EnvState, AnchorState, FieldState, EntropyState, DriftState

Flow:

ingest_environment()

ingest_anchor()

build_fields()

solve_gradient()

compute_entropy()

reinforce_gradient()

evaluate_drift()

Function: run_fae_simulation(t_start, t_end, dt)

Inputs: start time, end time, timestep

Outputs: time series of DriftState and FieldState

Description: Runs the kernel over a time window, logging gradients and drift.

4. Outputs and logging

Primary outputs:

Atomic fields: Phi_ext, Phi_int

Gradients: GradPhi, GradPhi_star

Entropy: S_A

Drift: v_eff, a_eff

Logging API:

log_state(t, EnvState, AnchorState, FieldState, EntropyState, DriftState)

